  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong></p><p>ALTERNATE 1 E<sub>T</sub> =« <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2GMm}{3R}-\\frac{GMm}{R}\"></span> =» <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-\\frac{1}{3}\\frac{GMm}{R}\"></span> ✔ E<sub>T </sub>&lt;0 hence it will not escape ✔   ALTERNATE 2 <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span>v<sup>2</sup> = <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2GMm}{3R}\"></span> ⇒ v = <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{\\frac{4GM}{3R}}\"></span> ✔</p>\n<p>v &lt; v<sub>esc</sub> hence it will not escape ✔</p>\n<p>Argument necessary to get second MP.<br/>Do not accept a bald statement that it will not escape.<br/>Allow ECF from MP1.</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"b.i\"><p><strong>b.i</strong></p><p>g = « <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{Δ {V}_{g}}{Δ r}\"></span> =» <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2.2 \\times  10^{6}}{\\frac{8.5 \\times  10^{6}}{2}}\"></span> ✔</p>\n<p>g = 0.52 «N kg<sup>−1</sup>» ✔</p>\n<p>Ignore negative sign</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"b.ii\"><p><strong>b.ii</strong></p><p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_03\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 3\" src=\"asset:fig_03\"/></figure></p>\n<p>« <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-\\frac{GM}{x}+\\frac{2GM}{3R} = -\\frac{2GM}{3R}+\\frac{GM}{R}\"></span> thus» x=3<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> ✔</p>\n<p>Circle of radius 3<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> drawn ✔</p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>A uniform, spherical planet P has mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> and radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span>.</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> </p><p>A projectile of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> is launched with kinetic energy <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2GMm}{3R}\"></span> from the surface of P.</p>\n<p>diagram not to scale</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Determine whether the projectile will escape the gravitational field of P.</p><p>[2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> </p><p>The surface of P is an equipotential surface E<sub>0</sub>. The dotted circle labeled E<sub>1</sub> is an equipotential line at a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{3R}{2}\"></span>from the centre of P. The potential difference between E<sub>1</sub> and E<sub>0</sub> is 2.2 × 10<sup>6</sup> J kg<sup>−1</sup>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p><p></p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b.i\"><p><strong>b.i</strong> </p><p>The radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> of P is 8.5 × 10<sup>6</sup> m.</p>\n<p>Estimate the magnitude of the gravitational field strength between E<sub>1</sub> and E<sub>0</sub>.</p><p>[2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b.ii\"><p><strong>b.ii</strong> </p><p>E<sub>2</sub> is an equipotential line such that the potential difference between E<sub>2</sub> and E<sub>1</sub> is also 2.2 × 10<sup>6</sup> J kg<sup>-1</sup>.</p>\n<p>Draw the equipotential line E<sub>2</sub> on the diagram.</p><p>[2]</p></section>"
  },
